        "department": null,
        "description": "This course is specifically designed to accommodate a diverse range of students with backgrounds in biology, medical science, pharmacology, bioinformatics, and computer science. The course is structured into three comprehensive sections: i) Challenges in Biomedical Sciences, ii) Intruduction to Machine Learning Techniques and iii) Solving Biomedical Problems using Machine Learning Techniques. Students will gain insights into the complexities of working with biomedical data and understand the unique requirements of applying machine learning techniques to solve real-world biomedical problems. In this course, students will work on case studies and real-life projects that require innovative applications of machine learning to solve problems in biological and health sciences.",
